-- title:
--   Γ₀(M) lies in the subgroup generated by T and q∣ b
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number and let $q$ be a non-zero natural number. Inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, consider the set consisting of the translation matrix $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ (Mathlib's `ModularGroup.T`) together with all $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ whose lower-left entry $\gamma_{1,0}$ is divisible by $M$ and whose upper-right entry $\gamma_{0,1}$ is divisible by $q$, the divisibilities being taken in $\mathbb{Z}$ with $M$ and $q$ cast from $\mathbb{N}$. The assertion is the inclusion of subgroups $\Gamma_0(M)\le\langle\{T\}\cup\{\gamma: M\mid \gamma_{1,0},\ q\mid\gamma_{0,1}\}\rangle$, where $\Gamma_0(M)$ is `CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M`, the subgroup of matrices whose lower-left entry vanishes in $\mathbb{Z}/M$, and the right-hand side is the subgroup generated by the displayed set. No primality is assumed of $q$, and $M$ is an arbitrary natural number; only $q\neq 0$ is required.
--
--   A generation statement for $\Gamma_0(M)$: every element of $\Gamma_0(M)$ is a product of translations and of elements of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-right entry is divisible by a prescribed non-zero integer $q$. It is used in the proof of [`CuspForm.eq_zero_of_prime_not_dvd_of_qCoeff_eq_zero`](thm.html#CuspForm.eq_zero_of_prime_not_dvd_of_qCoeff_eq_zero), where a vanishing property invariant under translations need only be checked on matrices with $q\mid b$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_Gamma0_le_closure_T_union_setOf_dvd.lean

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.CongruenceSubgroups

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0_le_closure_T_union_setOf_dvd (M : ℕ) {q : ℕ} (hq : q ≠ 0) :
    CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M ≤ Subgroup.closure
      ({ModularGroup.T} ∪ {γ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ |
        (M : ℤ) ∣ (γ : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℤ) 1 0 ∧ (q : ℤ) ∣ (γ : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℤ) 0 1}) := by sorry
